    fix(types): GAP-043 — clear the two mypy arg-type drifts in src/ (template + shim_loop)
    
    Gate 7 (`uv run --with mypy mypy src/`) reported 4 errors instead of the
    3-stub-only envelope: two real `arg-type` mismatches, both annotation-only,
    both invisible to ruff/CI (neither runs mypy) and both introduced by the
    previous tick's commits.
    
    1. src/h3_shim/templates/py/main.py — `_summarize_validation_errors` was
       annotated `list[dict[str, Any]]` while its only caller feeds it
       `RequestValidationError.errors()`, which pydantic types as
       `Sequence[ErrorDetails]`. Introduced by 553620a (DF-H3-SHIM-FOREMAN-3,
       tick #379). Widened to `Sequence[Mapping[str, Any]]` (+ the
       `collections.abc` import) so the signature matches the real producer.
    
    2. src/h3_shim/shim_loop.py — `_format_pydantic_error` was annotated
       `dict[str, Any]` while `_first_error_line` feeds it `exc.errors()[0]`
       (`ErrorDetails`). Introduced by 8adce0e (DF2-H3-SHIM-2, this tick).
       Widened to `Mapping[str, Any]`.
    
    Runtime behaviour is unchanged: both helpers only read via `.get()`/indexing,
    which `Mapping` supports, and the annotations of the scaffold template are
    never evaluated by the generated project (`from __future__ import
    annotations`). No new dependency, no logic change.
    
    Gates (fresh, at the committed tree): `uv run --with mypy mypy src/` -> 3
    errors in 3 files, all the known import-untyped stubs (types-PyYAML x2,
    jsonschema x1) = back inside the documented envelope; `.venv/bin/python -m
    pytest -q` -> 369 passed; `.venv/bin/ruff check .` rc=0;
    `.venv/bin/ruff format --check .` -> 48 files already formatted.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
